  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25145768",
      "title": "Introducing Client-Side Data Fetching (And When To Use It)",
      "lectureOrder": 286,
      "videoOrder": 267,
      "sourceHash": "c695906edf1e953c3580fa527a28f1f32db349a30192a7c93e9d1caa8f6eae47",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.22,
          "end": 3.92,
          "en": "Now that we learned a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.92,
          "end": 8.21,
          "en": "about page pre rendering and data pre-fetching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.21,
          "end": 13.04,
          "en": "in various ways, I wanna conclude this course section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 13.04,
          "end": 16.7,
          "en": "by having another look at client site data fetching.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.7,
          "end": 20.16,
          "en": "So basically the opposite of what we did thus far",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.16,
          "end": 23.06,
          "en": "where we talked about fetching and preparing data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.06,
          "end": 26.32,
          "en": "on the server or during the build process.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.32,
          "end": 30.74,
          "en": "When building next JS applications, you will sometimes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.74,
          "end": 35.31,
          "en": "have data which just doesn't need to be pre-rendered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 35.31,
          "end": 38.35,
          "en": "or which can't be pre-rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 38.35,
          "end": 42.32,
          "en": "Examples would be data that changes with high frequency.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 42.32,
          "end": 44.89,
          "en": "So for example, if you have stock data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 44.89,
          "end": 47.55,
          "en": "which you show on some page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 47.55,
          "end": 51.97,
          "en": "and that data changes multiple times every second,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 51.97,
          "end": 55.97,
          "en": "pre fetching and pre rendering might not make too much sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 55.97,
          "end": 59.35,
          "en": "because you will always see outdated data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 59.35,
          "end": 61.65,
          "en": "when you visit this page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 61.65,
          "end": 64.37,
          "en": "So in such a case, just showing a loading spinner",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 64.37,
          "end": 65.92,
          "en": "when you visit the page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 65.92,
          "end": 69.48,
          "en": "and then fetching the very latest data for you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 69.48,
          "end": 71.45,
          "en": "and maybe updating that data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.45,
          "end": 75.56,
          "en": "in the background then might be the best user experience.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.56,
          "end": 79.2,
          "en": "Another example would be highly user-specific data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.2,
          "end": 83.18,
          "en": "For example, the last orders in an online shop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 83.18,
          "end": 86.87,
          "en": "If you are in your account and your user profile",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.87,
          "end": 89.12,
          "en": "and you view that data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 89.12,
          "end": 91.97,
          "en": "that could be an example where we don't really need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91.97,
          "end": 94.28999999999999,
          "en": "to pre-render a page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 94.28999999999999,
          "end": 96.9,
          "en": "Definitely not for search engines",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 96.9,
          "end": 100.77000000000001,
          "en": "because they won't see your private profile,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 100.77000000000001,
          "end": 104.4,
          "en": "and also not necessarily for the user experience",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 104.4,
          "end": 107.59,
          "en": "because if we go to this page, we might be more than fine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 107.59,
          "end": 111.25,
          "en": "with just waiting a second for the data to be loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 111.25,
          "end": 114.75,
          "en": "on the client and having a quicker navigation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 114.75,
          "end": 117.11,
          "en": "to the page might be more important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 117.11,
          "end": 120.73,
          "en": "than having the data available right from the start.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 120.73,
          "end": 124.13,
          "en": "Or considered a case that you have partial data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 124.13,
          "end": 126.92,
          "en": "So let's say you have like a dashboard page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 126.92,
          "end": 129.62,
          "en": "with a lots of different pieces of data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 129.62,
          "end": 133.05,
          "en": "lots of different kinds of data, in such a case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 133.05,
          "end": 135.87,
          "en": "loading all these different pieces, which make up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 135.87,
          "end": 139.63,
          "en": "the overall dashboard might just slow down the request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 139.63,
          "end": 141.62,
          "en": "if you do that on the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 141.62,
          "end": 144.99,
          "en": "and pre rendering it statically during build time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 144.99,
          "end": 146.59,
          "en": "might also not make sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 146.59,
          "end": 150.37,
          "en": "because it's personal data or because it's changing a lot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 150.37,
          "end": 154.43,
          "en": "So in such a scenario, it would again, probably make sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 154.43,
          "end": 157.37,
          "en": "to fetch that data on the client,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 157.37,
          "end": 160.69,
          "en": "so from inside the regular react app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 160.69,
          "end": 164.48,
          "en": "once a user navigated to that page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 164.48,
          "end": 166.59,
          "en": "And these are just some examples.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 166.59,
          "end": 170.07,
          "en": "But there can be used cases like those here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 170.07,
          "end": 174.55,
          "en": "where pre fetching the data and pre-generating the page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 174.55,
          "end": 177.99,
          "en": "with that data, might just not really work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 177.99,
          "end": 180.59,
          "en": "or might not make too much sense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 180.59,
          "end": 184.41,
          "en": "And in such cases, it might make the most sense to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 184.41,
          "end": 188.28,
          "en": "the traditional approach of writing some code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 188.28,
          "end": 193.04,
          "en": "in your react components may be with user fact and fetch,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 193.04,
          "end": 197.28,
          "en": "Q fetch data from some API from inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 197.28,
          "end": 200.42000000000002,
          "en": "the client side react application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 200.42000000000002,
          "end": 203.35,
          "en": "So not from inside get static props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 203.35,
          "end": 207.09,
          "en": "or get service side props, but really from inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 207.09,
          "end": 210.42000000000002,
          "en": "the component, so that this code only runs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 210.42000000000002,
          "end": 215.12,
          "en": "once the code executes in the client, not on the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 215.12,
          "end": 216.98,
          "en": "And therefore that's what we're now going",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 216.98,
          "end": 218.513,
          "en": "to take a closer look at.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
